      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      278.55,
      484.9,
      292.61
    ],
    "text": "antecedents and age of the offender, public interest must prevail. \"",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      309.75,
      527.26,
      323.75
    ],
    "text": "In the case of Don Percy Nanayakkara v The Republic of Sri Lanka [1993]",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle",
      "BookmanOldStyle-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      330.87,
      256.37,
      344.87
    ],
    "text": "1 SLR 71 the Court held that:",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      361.95,
      526.78,
      376.01
    ],
    "text": "\u201cIn assessing punishment, the Court has to consider the matter from the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      383.07,
      526.82,
      397.13
    ],
    "text": "point of both the offender and the public. The accused had held high public",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      404.19,
      526.66,
      418.25
    ],
    "text": "office and exercised extensive statutory power in conducting public",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      425.31,
      527.01,
      439.37
    ],
    "text": "examinations in this country. These examinations have to be conducted",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      446.43,
      526.8,
      460.49
    ],
    "text": "fairly and the results declared accurately. Thousands of students who face",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      467.57,
      526.7,
      481.63
    ],
    "text": "public examinations, every year, should have complete confidence in the",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      488.69,
      526.74,
      502.75
    ],
    "text": "fairness and accuracy of every process of the examinations. The accused",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      509.93,
      526.84,
      523.99
    ],
    "text": "has subverted the very basis of this confidence by his conduct in",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      531.05,
      526.7,
      545.11
    ],
    "text": "dishonestly showing favour to persons with whom he was acquainted.",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      552.17,
      526.7,
      566.23
    ],
    "text": "Therefore, public interest demands that he should be imposed a deterrent",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      573.29,
      179.78,
      587.35
    ],
    "text": "punishment.\u201d",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      78.02,
      604.37,
      527.26,
      618.37
    ],
    "text": "In the case of Attorney General v. Mendis [1995] 1 Sri L.R. 138 it was held:",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle",
      "BookmanOldStyle-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      635.57,
      526.68,
      649.63
    ],
    "text": "\u201cIn our view once an accused is found guilty and convicted on his own",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      656.72,
      526.66,
      670.78
    ],
    "text": "plea, or after trial, the Trial Judge has a difficult function to perform. That",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      677.84,
      526.72,
      691.9
    ],
    "text": "is to decide what sentence is to be imposed on the accused who has been",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      99.38,
      698.96,
      526.78,
      713.02
    ],
    "text": "convicted. In doing so he has to consider the point of view of the accused",
    "fonts": [
      "BookmanOldStyle-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
